users/PiCode9560/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T03:50:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T06:13:30Z","body":"> when using Jolt Physics, nothing happens when trying to set an impulse (on a single point or all points).\r\n\r\nI tested it. It does work, but need a very large force for it to work. Apparently, in jolt physics, the more vertices added, the greater the force needed (for apply impulse and force).\r\n\r\n<strike> @jrouwe do you think this is an intentional behaviour? The code looks like it work the same as godot physics, but on godot physics the force seems consistent no mater how many vertices there are. </strike>\r\n\r\nEdit: \r\n@Calinou \r\nActually, I figured it out, the soft body mass is set to 0 on jolt by default, if you set it to 1 it will work just like godot physics.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885561204/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910228113","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100463#issuecomment-2910228113","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100463","id":2910228113,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tdo6R","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://ap